# Everything the image does not need. Two reasons this matters beyond image size:
# the build context is uploaded to the Docker daemon before the build starts, so a
# 400 MB .venv makes every build slow; and anything copied in is visible inside the
# container, so excluding it is also about not shipping what was never meant to ship.

# The local environment -- large, and platform-specific to Windows in any case.
.venv/
venv/

# Version control and editor state.
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Caches and build output.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Training-only material. The service loads a fitted artefact; it never reads the
# CSVs, never re-fits, and has no use for the pipeline. Excluding data/ also keeps
# the training set out of a distributed image, which is worth doing by default.
data/
scripts/
tests/
docs/

# The training report is the pipeline's output, not the service's input. Only
# artefacts/titre_model.json is copied in, explicitly, by the Dockerfile.
artefacts/training_report.json

# Notes and specifications that the running service does not consult.
*.md
!README.md
inference_server_spec.yml
